1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,021
An old man in the temple held a baby and told

2
00:00:02,041 --> 00:00:03,541
the mother one dark sentence.

3
00:00:04,182 --> 00:00:07,203
Yea, a sword shall pierce through thy own soul

4
00:00:07,403 --> 00:00:07,743
also.

5
00:00:07,843 --> 00:00:08,684
Simeon told Mary.

6
00:00:09,784 --> 00:00:12,485
Some thirty years later, the sword lands.

7
00:00:13,065 --> 00:00:15,606
Now there stood by the cross of Jesus his mother.

8
00:00:15,746 --> 00:00:17,267
Close enough to watch her son die.

9
00:00:18,668 --> 00:00:21,049
Jesus looks down, sees her wound, and turns

10
00:00:21,089 --> 00:00:21,549
to bind it.

11
00:00:22,089 --> 00:00:24,450
When Jesus therefore saw his mother, and the

12
00:00:24,490 --> 00:00:27,471
disciple standing by, whom he loved, he saith

13
00:00:27,551 --> 00:00:31,273
unto his mother, Woman, behold thy son!

14
00:00:31,873 --> 00:00:35,594
Then saith he to the disciple, Behold thy mother!

15
00:00:36,215 --> 00:00:38,996
And from that hour that disciple took her unto

16
00:00:39,036 --> 00:00:39,776
his own home.

17
00:00:39,936 --> 00:00:41,317
He gave her the disciple he loved.

18
00:00:42,037 --> 00:00:42,377
A son.

19
00:00:42,397 --> 00:00:43,498
A home.

20
00:00:43,598 --> 00:00:46,179
While judgment fell on him, he cared for someone

21
00:00:46,259 --> 00:00:46,559
else.

22
00:00:47,579 --> 00:00:49,100
That is who is dying there.

23
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:50,821
Your wound is not invisible to him.

24
00:00:51,701 --> 00:00:53,041
He sees it from the cross.

25
00:00:53,162 --> 00:00:54,262
Stand where Mary stood.

26
00:00:55,182 --> 00:00:57,823
The Son who saw her will behold you, and bind

27
00:00:57,863 --> 00:00:58,684
what the sword tore.
